{"title":"2026 INMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h1>\n<p>Two decks <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cards each are placed on a table at noon. Every minute thereafter, we pick the topmost cards of the decks, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/5/1a50f85686fe7cb27b1ae676014e18fc9e46e9bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\in A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/9/999e49d223e45c4430a52817a56531e24d7bcb3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b\\in B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />, and perform a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/7/287c274ed827e94952eebf82af7f16a15f5975da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$duel$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>For any two cards <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/5/1a50f85686fe7cb27b1ae676014e18fc9e46e9bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\in A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c4a5415d1e2419d839d8bd4d5045549c441bd4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b \\in B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />, each time <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> duel, the outcome remains the same and is independent of other duels. A duel has three possible outcomes:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/3/7f3b4ea3b8abe9ced6095c7d75f207a1127ee843.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"7\" /> If a card wins, it is placed back on the top of its deck and the losing card is placed at the bottom of its deck.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/3/7f3b4ea3b8abe9ced6095c7d75f207a1127ee843.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"7\" /> If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are evenly matched, they are both removed from their respective decks.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/3/7f3b4ea3b8abe9ced6095c7d75f207a1127ee843.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"7\" /> If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> do not interact with each other, then both are placed at the bottom of their respective decks.\n</p><p>The sequence of duels ends when both decks are empty, otherwise it goes on forever. Prove that either such a sequence of duels continues infinitely, or the sequence ends at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/9/509f7aafdacc5424492342c2b0d23ca9c2f177bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$356$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> hours after the first duel.\n</p>\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h1>\n<p>This page needs a solution! Please help by adding one.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO\" title=\"2026 INMO\">2026 INMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems\" title=\"2026 INMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2026 INMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"